# Correctness-critical paths must stay visible to git.
#
# An ignore rule does not untrack files that are already committed, but it does
# hide every newly created file at that path: `git status`, `git diff` and
# `git add` all skip it silently, so a test or CI definition written on such a
# host never reaches a branch and no reviewer ever sees it. Reproduced on a
# developer machine on 2026-09-29 with throwaway probe files.
#
# Do not re-add any of the following, here or in a per-host .git/info/exclude:
#   .github/  test/  tests/  **/test/  **/tests/
#   *_test.exs  *_test.ex  *_test.py  test_*.py  test_*.exs  conftest.py
#   .gitignore  .gitattributes
# The 'ignore-hygiene' job in .github/workflows/elixir_ci.yml enforces this.
